{"name":"Dover Surf","hex":"#aec3c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"surf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Waves that break on an ocean shoreline.","An instance or session of riding a surfboard in the surf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ride a wave on a surfboard; to pursue or take part in the sport of surfing.","To surf at a specified place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Surf (detergent)","blocks":[{"text":"Surf is a British brand of laundry detergent manufactured and marketed around the world by Unilever, except in the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico, where it has been owned by Sun Products since 2008."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Surf-logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surf_(detergent)"},{"title":"Dover","blocks":[{"text":"Dover is a town, major ferry port and civil parish in Kent, England. It faces France across the Strait of Dover, the narrowest part of the English Channel at 33 kilometres (21 mi) from Cap Gris-Nez in France. It lies southeast of Canterbury and east of Maidstone. The town is the administrative centre of the Dover District and home of the Port of Dover. In 2024 it had an estimated population of 44,209."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg/330px-Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dover_Town_Hall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2321356.jpg/500px-Dover_Town_Hall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2321356.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6